{"body": "This is a minor feature improvement. The background is that we are using RewriteTablePathProcedure to convert Hive tables to Iceberg tables, as detailed in #12762. RewriteTablePathProcedure generates a file-list file, and I need to manually clean up this file after each conversion. I understand that the file-list is mainly used to check data integrity, but since it is not essential for metadata, I believe allowing users to decide whether to generate this file would offer greater flexibility.", "date": "2025-04-18T23:48:27Z", "hash": "sha256:30d55fdf9185611cd028", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#12844", "meta": {"additions": 88, "base": "main", "closed_at": "2025-07-25T23:30:22Z", "comments": 26, "deletions": 13, "draft": false, "files": ["api/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/actions/RewriteTablePath.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/actions/BaseRewriteTablePath.java", "spark/v4.0/spark-extensions/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/extensions/TestRewriteTablePathProcedure.java", "spark/v4.0/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/actions/RewriteTablePathSparkAction.java", "spark/v4.0/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/procedures/RewriteTablePathProcedure.java"], "labels": ["API", "spark", "core", "stale"], "n_files": 5, "number": 12844, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "reviews": [{"at": "2025-04-19T06:18:39Z", "by": "szehon-ho", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-19T07:08:49Z", "by": "slfan1989", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-19T07:15:34Z", "by": "slfan1989", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-21T17:02:24Z", "by": "dramaticlly", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-22T01:51:06Z", "by": "slfan1989", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-23T03:10:10Z", "by": "manuzhang", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-05-28T15:06:25Z", "by": "manuzhang", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-03T15:21:09Z", "by": "slfan1989", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-10T01:49:30Z", "by": "slfan1989", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-10T15:00:27Z", "by": "dramaticlly", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-11T00:45:32Z", "by": "slfan1989", "state": "COMMENTED"}], "state": "closed", "thumbs_up": 0, "updated_at": "2025-07-25T23:34:44Z"}, "people": ["slfan1989"], "refs": ["gh:apache/iceberg#12762"], "source": "github", "title": "Spark: Add 'skip_file_list' option to RewriteTablePathProcedure for optional file-list generation", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/12844"}
{"body": "This change prevents calling close() on FileIO during the cleanup of Spark's broadcast variable when memoryStore.remove(blockId) is called. Closing FileIO can unintentionally shut down shared resources—such as a shared connection pool—when S3FileIO is backed by the Apache HTTPClient. Calling close() will trigger the shutdown of the HttpClientConnectionManager, leading to request failures if other instances are still in use.\nFixes: #12858, #12046", "date": "2025-04-22T17:21:02Z", "hash": "sha256:5469307ff04f42592120", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#12868", "meta": {"additions": 14, "association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "base": "main", "closes": [12858], "comments": 16, "deletions": 18, "draft": false, "files": ["spark/v3.4/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/SerializableTableWithSize.java", "spark/v3.4/spark/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/TestTableSerialization.java", "spark/v3.5/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/SerializableTableWithSize.java", "spark/v3.5/spark/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/TestTableSerialization.java"], "labels": ["spark", "not-stale"], "last_commit": "2025-04-22T19:15:20Z", "n_files": 4, "number": 12868, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "requested": ["amogh-jahagirdar", "danielcweeks", "nastra", "huaxingao"], "reviews": [{"at": "2025-04-23T06:25:05Z", "by": "bk-mz", "state": "APPROVED"}, {"at": "2025-04-23T16:13:44Z", "by": "singhpk234", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-24T00:34:35Z", "by": "dramaticlly", "state": "APPROVED"}, {"at": "2025-04-24T03:44:45Z", "by": "xiaoxuandev", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-05-08T14:14:31Z", "by": "nastra", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-05-08T14:16:10Z", "by": "nastra", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-05-08T14:22:03Z", "by": "mgmarino", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-05-08T14:58:34Z", "by": "nastra", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-05-08T15:05:58Z", "by": "mgmarino", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-05-08T19:44:20Z", "by": "xiaoxuandev", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-05-08T19:51:58Z", "by": "xiaoxuandev", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-05-31T00:51:07Z", "by": "yyanyy", "state": "APPROVED"}], "state": "open", "thumbs_up": 0, "updated_at": "2026-01-15T09:00:37Z"}, "people": ["xiaoxuandev"], "refs": ["gh:apache/iceberg#12858", "gh:apache/iceberg#12046", "gh:apache/iceberg#12858"], "source": "github", "title": "Spark: Avoid closing deserialized copies of shared resources like FileIO", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/12868"}
{"body": "RewriteTablePath incremental mode limits rewrite/copy plan to those between two snapshots. However, the returned copy plan ignores this limitation and includes all referenced files by these snapshots, even those not modified between the two snapshots. This leads to unnecessary copies.  This patch allows of rewriting table path to use snapshots to filter both\n\nadded_snapshot_id in ManifestFile\nsnapshot_id in ManifestEntry\n\nIt help avoid repeated copy of same data files when manifest rewrite happens in between incremental copy. Manifest rewrite will only change added snapshot id for manifest, but data files remain the same and it shall not be copied over repeatedly.\nIf you can help take a look @flyrain @szehon-ho", "date": "2025-04-24T02:38:38Z", "hash": "sha256:c747b38ec3b0e8ae3ba3", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#12885", "meta": {"additions": 312, "base": "main", "closed_at": "2025-06-13T03:50:07Z", "comments": 14, "deletions": 29, "draft": false, "files": ["core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/RewriteTablePathUtil.java", "spark/v3.4/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/actions/RewriteTablePathSparkAction.java", "spark/v3.4/spark/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/actions/TestRewriteTablePathsAction.java", "spark/v3.5/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/actions/RewriteTablePathSparkAction.java", "spark/v3.5/spark/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/actions/TestRewriteTablePathsAction.java", "spark/v4.0/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/actions/RewriteTablePathSparkAction.java", "spark/v4.0/spark/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/actions/TestRewriteTablePathsAction.java"], "labels": ["spark", "core"], "merged_at": "2025-06-13T03:50:07Z", "merged_by": "szehon-ho", "n_files": 7, "number": 12885, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "reviews": [{"at": "2025-06-03T01:16:23Z", "by": "szehon-ho", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-11T05:07:37Z", "by": "dramaticlly", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-11T23:42:04Z", "by": "szehon-ho", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-12T15:52:24Z", "by": "szehon-ho", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-12T15:55:30Z", "by": "szehon-ho", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-12T23:39:48Z", "by": "dramaticlly", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-13T03:49:21Z", "by": "szehon-ho", "state": "APPROVED"}], "state": "merged", "thumbs_up": 0, "updated_at": "2026-10-30T21:40:51Z"}, "people": ["dramaticlly"], "refs": [], "source": "github", "title": "Spark: RewriteTablePath: filter content files by snapshotId", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/12885"}
{"body": "Following the update on the spec regarding source-id and source-ids (thanks again @Fokko 😄 ), here's the PR to introduce source-ids field in partition spec.\nA few notes:\n\nInternal representation is now based on source-ids\nSerialization/deserialization supports source-id and source-ids elements in the json (exclusive), both populating source-ids internal representation (as List<Integer>)\nThe TestPartitionSpecParser is still testing source-id, but also source-ids parsing, and neither source-id and source-ids presence (throwing IllegalArgumentException in that case)\nFor backward compatibility (especially for the transforms), source id is still supported (using the first element in the internal representation) and some methods have been flagged as deprecated to encourage use of source ids.", "date": "2025-04-25T09:25:09Z", "hash": "sha256:c9c10cde5518e9d71c0f", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#12897", "meta": {"additions": 1123, "association": "MEMBER", "base": "main", "comments": 36, "deletions": 139, "draft": false, "files": [".palantir/revapi.yml", "api/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/PartitionField.java", "api/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/PartitionSpec.java", "api/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/SortField.java", "api/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/SortOrder.java", "api/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/UnboundPartitionSpec.java", "api/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/UnboundSortOrder.java", "api/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/transforms/Transforms.java", "api/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/TestPartitionSpecValidation.java", "api/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/TestSortField.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/BaseUpdatePartitionSpec.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/PartitionSpecParser.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/Partitioning.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/SortOrderParser.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/TableMetadata.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/util/SortOrderUtil.java", "core/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/TestPartitionSpecParser.java", "core/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/TestSortOrderParser.java", "core/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/TestTableMetadata.java", "core/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/TestUpdatePartitionSpec.java"], "labels": ["API", "core", "not-stale"], "last_commit": "2026-11-10T10:42:45Z", "n_files": 20, "number": 12897, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "requested": ["Fokko", "rdblue"], "reviews": [{"at": "2025-04-25T12:47:00Z", "by": "ajantha-bhat", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T13:09:32Z", "by": "jbonofre", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T13:11:15Z", "by": "jbonofre", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T13:11:44Z", "by": "jbonofre", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T13:23:12Z", "by": "jbonofre", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T14:27:18Z", "by": "ajantha-bhat", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T14:35:10Z", "by": "jbonofre", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T15:20:46Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T15:21:49Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T15:25:14Z", "by": "jbonofre", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T15:27:24Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T15:51:52Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T15:58:59Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T16:01:07Z", "by": "jbonofre", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T16:01:53Z", "by": "jbonofre", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T16:04:31Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T16:06:18Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T16:09:36Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-25T16:11:00Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-26T03:47:13Z", "by": "jbonofre", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-04-26T03:52:51Z", "by